    "controller_support": "full",
    "detailed_description": "<h1>Still in Development</h1><p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Huge Update Coming Soon!</h2>Though Dark Data is not in Early Access on Steam, it should have been, and is still in Full-Time Development. It has received nearly three more years of development since the launch of version 1, and version 2 is nearly complete! Dark Data has been worked on from the ground up and has gotten a lot of additional content, including a story campaign mode! I really appreciate all the support over the years and am extremely excited to release the mega-update. If you want to check out version 1 now or wishlist and wait for version 2, it means a lot!<br><br>Join the discord and ping me if you'd like access to internal Beta multiplayer builds!<br></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1>In a world driven by blackmail, time is not money...crime is. Do you have what it takes to uncover the truth while staring at the business end of a gun? Dark Data is a local multiplayer FPS based on the unreleased mid-nineties film of the same name. Square off in diverse locations with up to 3 friends and cutthroat digital Artificial Intelligence in full 360 degree combat. Coming Summer 2019 to your home entertainment system.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Game Types</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Deathmatch<br></li><li> Team Deathmatch<br></li><li> HOLD YOUR DEATH<br></li><li> Capture The Floppy<br></li><li> Occupation</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Up to 8 Combatants per Match</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> 1-4 Players<br></li><li> 1-7 AI</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Kill with Variety and Style</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>19 Unique Weapons<br></li><li>11 Multiplayer Maps<br></li><li>State-of-the-Art Character Creator<br></li><li>Multitudes of Outfits and Accessories </li></ul><br>Strive to become the leader on the Dark Data DIRTcoin leaderboards! Will you fight along the Corruptors to dismantle the DIRTcoin economy, or side with the government-backed Verification Agents who keep the system thriving? The choice is yours!",
    "about_the_game": "In a world driven by blackmail, time is not money...crime is. Do you have what it takes to uncover the truth while staring at the business end of a gun? Dark Data is a local multiplayer FPS based on the unreleased mid-nineties film of the same name. Square off in diverse locations with up to 3 friends and cutthroat digital Artificial Intelligence in full 360 degree combat. Coming Summer 2019 to your home entertainment system.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Game Types</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Deathmatch<br></li><li> Team Deathmatch<br></li><li> HOLD YOUR DEATH<br></li><li> Capture The Floppy<br></li><li> Occupation</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Up to 8 Combatants per Match</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> 1-4 Players<br></li><li> 1-7 AI</li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Kill with Variety and Style</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>19 Unique Weapons<br></li><li>11 Multiplayer Maps<br></li><li>State-of-the-Art Character Creator<br></li><li>Multitudes of Outfits and Accessories </li></ul><br>Strive to become the leader on the Dark Data DIRTcoin leaderboards! Will you fight along the Corruptors to dismantle the DIRTcoin economy, or side with the government-backed Verification Agents who keep the system thriving? The choice is yours!",
    "short_description": "In a world driven by blackmail, time is not money...crime is. Do you have what it takes to uncover the truth while staring at the business end of a gun? Dark Data is a local multiplayer FPS based on the unreleased mid-nineties film of the same name.",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French, German, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese - Portugal, Russian, Simplified Chinese, Spanish - Latin America<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
    "reviews": "\u201cThis is a well-made game. It is unfinished obviously. But, you need to check it out soon.\u201d<br>BrandonChoveyDotNet<br><br>\u201cDark Data feels especially novel, as its clearly a hat tip to a distinctive, platform-specific style of FPS, namely, Nintendo 64 classics like GoldenEye 007 and Perfect Dark\u201d<br>Shaun Prescott , PC Gamer<br>",
